  "reading": "The 181° and 192° frames show the same trunk next to the blue-sign pier, a tree well and continuous grey paving outside the railing. The independent 186° frame shows the same order, but its unadjusted ray misses the paired tree root by about 1.97 m. The 161° trunk and the upper projecting facade are useful for identifying the sequence, with correspondence or pose uncertainty too large for an exact wall-foot limit.",
